content='<think>\nOkay, I need to generate an Ansible Playbook based on the user\'s instructions. Let me go through the requirements carefully.\n\nFirst, the playbook must start with \'---\', which is standard for YAML files. It should be a valid Ansible Playbook, conforming to yamllint and ansible-lint. Also, it needs to be structured to fit into an Ansible Role under the tasks directory, like tasks/main.yml.\n\nThere are three tasks to include:\n\n1. **Task 1: Restart RKE2 Service**\n   - Use the `service` module to restart the service.\n   - Notify a handler when the service is restarted.\n   - The service name is from `rke2_service_name` and the node name from `rke2_node_name`.\n\n2. **Task 2: Wait for Nodes to be Ready**\n   - Use the `shell` module to run a kubectl command.\n   - Check if all nodes are in a Ready state.\n   - Retry up to 100 times with 15-second delays.\n   - Delegated to `active_server` or first server in `rke2_servers_group_name`.\n   - Runs once.\n\n3. **Task 3: Wait for Pods to be Ready**\n   - Similar to Task 2 but for pods.\n   - Only runs if `rke2_wait_for_all_pods_to_be_ready` is true and not in check mode.\n\nI need to make sure each task is correctly formatted in YAML, using the specified modules and variables. Also, the tasks should be in the exact order provided.\n\nI\'ll structure each task with the appropriate module, args, and any necessary conditions. For tasks 2 and 3, I\'ll include the `delegate_to` parameter and set `register` and `until` for the retries. For the conditional in Task 3, I\'ll use `when`.\n\nI must avoid adding any hosts, vars, or playbook-level headers since it\'s meant for a role. Only the tasks should be included, starting with \'---\'.\n\nLet me double-check each task for correct syntax and variable usage. Make sure the YAML is valid and adheres to linting standards.\n\nFinally, I\'ll compile all tasks into the playbook, ensuring the correct order and structure.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Restart the RKE2 service\n  service:\n    name: "{{ rke2_service_name }}"\n    state: restarted\n    node_name: "{{ rke2_node_name }}"\n  notify: Service (re)started\n\n- name: Wait for all nodes to be ready\n  shell: >\n    "{{ rke2_data_path }}/bin/kubectl --kubeconfig=/etc/rancher/rke2/rke2.yaml get nodes -o json | jq -r \'.items[].status.conditions[] | select(.type == "Ready") | select(.status == "True") | .message\' | wc -l"\n  register: ready_node_count\n  until: ready_node_count.stdout == "{{ rke2_cluster_group_name|length }}"\n  retries: 100\n  delay: 15\n  delegate_to: "{{ rke2_active_server | default(rke2_servers_group_name[0]) }}"\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Wait for all pods to be ready\n  shell: >\n    "{{ rke2_data_path }}/bin/kubectl --kubeconfig=/etc/rancher/rke2/rke2.yaml get pods --all-namespaces -o json | jq -r \'[.items[] | select(.status.phase != "Running" and .status.phase != "Succeeded") | .metadata.name] | length\'\n  register: pending_pods_count\n  until: pending_pods_count.stdout == "0"\n  retries: 100\n  delay: 15\n  delegate_to: "{{ rke2_active_server | default(rke2_servers_group_name[0]) }}"\n  run_once: true\n  when: rke2_wait_for_all_pods_to_be_ready and not ansible_check_mode\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-11T05:41:10.891166346Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 14749529146, 'load_duration': 2701899012, 'prompt_eval_count': 673, 'prompt_eval_duration': 420939235, 'eval_count': 840, 'eval_duration': 11625480035, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--7d64343d-08b0-41c5-9f5d-f3671019ad31-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 673, 'output_tokens': 840, 'total_tokens': 1513}
