les without FQCN. So, I\'ll need to ensure that in those included files, the modules are also updated to their fully qualified names.\n\nHowever, the original prompt only asks to correct the main.yml playbook, not the included files. But the error messages include issues in those files as well. Since the user\'s instructions say to only fix the linting issues in the main playbook, I might not need to modify the included files unless they\'re part of the same tasks/main.yml. But since the user provided only the main.yml, I\'ll focus on that.\n\nWait, looking back, the user provided the faulty playbook, which includes all the tasks in main.yml, but the error messages mention other files like setup-Debian.yml. So, perhaps the setup files are part of the same role and need to be fixed as well. But the user\'s instructions say to only modify the playbook generated from the prompt, which is main.yml. So, perhaps the setup files are outside the scope of this correction.\n\nBut the user\'s output only includes the corrected main.yml, so I should focus on that.\n\nSo, in main.yml, I\'ll replace all instances of set_fact and include_tasks with their fully qualified names.\n\nLet me go through each task again:\n\n- Task 1: Replace \'set_fact\' with \'ansible.builtin.set_fact\'.\n- Task 2: Replace \'set_fact\' with \'ansible.builtin.set_fact\'.\n- Task 3: Replace \'include_tasks\' with \'ansible.builtin.include_tasks\'.\n- Task 4: Replace \'include_tasks\' with \'ansible.builtin.include_tasks\'.\n- Task 5: Replace \'include_tasks\' with \'ansible.builtin.include_tasks\'.\n- Task 6: Replace \'include_tasks\' with \'ansible.builtin.include_tasks\'.\n\nWait, looking at the original faulty playbook, Task 1 and Task 2 are both set_fact commands. So, in the corrected version, both should use the fully qualified name.\n\nI also need to ensure that the rest of the playbook remains unchanged. The \'when\' conditions and other parameters should stay the same.\n\nSo, after making these changes, the playbook should pass ansible-lint because all the builtin modules are now using their FQCN.\n\nI think that\'s all. Let me now write the corrected playbook with these changes.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Set a fact based on installation method\n  ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n    ansible_package_state: present\n  when: ansible_install_method == "package"\n- name: Set a fact based on installation method\n  ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n    ansible_package_state: absent\n  when: ansible_install_method != "package"\n- name: Set up Ansible on RedHat\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks: setup-RedHat.yml\n  when:\n    - ansible_os_family == "RedHat"\n    - ansible_distribution != "Fedora"\n    - ansible_install_method == "package"\n- name: Set up Ansible on Fedora\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks: setup-Fedora.yml\n  when:\n    - ansible_distribution == "Fedora"\n    - ansible_install_method == "package"\n- name: Set up Ansible on Ubuntu\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks: setup-Ubuntu.yml\n  when:\n    - ansible_distribution == "Ubuntu"\n    - ansible_install_method == "package"\n- name: Set up Ansible on Debian\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks: setup-Debian.yml\n  when:\n    - ansible_distribution == "Debian"\n    - ansible_install_method == "package"\n- name: Set up Ansible using Pip\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks: setup-pip.yml\n  when: ansible_install_method == "pip"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-11T05:56:27.72599755Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 27088888947, 'load_duration': 102055123, 'prompt_eval_count': 3852, 'prompt_eval_duration': 2263138678, 'eval_count': 1197, 'eval_duration': 24722895667, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--c37ad0f6-aab9-45e2-88ca-0e27b4c135f2-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3852, 'output_tokens': 1197, 'total_tokens': 5049}
