ssue is that the \'when\' is part of a list or another structure where a boolean is expected. Let me check the YAML structure.\n\nLooking at the original playbook, the \'block\' under \'Install using package\' has a \'when\' condition, and inside it, the \'Install repository for RedHat\' task has its own \'when\' condition. So, the structure is:\n\n- name: Install using package\n  block:\n    - name: Install repository for RedHat\n      get_url:\n        ...\n      vars:\n        ...\n      when: ansible_os_family == "RedHat"\n\n    - name: Configure debian\n      block:\n        ...\n      when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"\n\nSo, each task inside the block has its own \'when\' condition. That should be correct.\n\nWait, perhaps the issue is that the \'when\' is not a boolean but a string, but that\'s not the case because \'ansible_os_family == "RedHat"\' evaluates to true or false.\n\nI\'m a bit stuck on the first error. Maybe I should proceed with the line length fix and see if that resolves the issue, or perhaps the truthy value error is related to another part.\n\nWait, looking at the \'Install versioned hashicorp product using package\' task, the \'when\' is:\n\nwhen: hashicorp_products is defined\n\nWhich is correct because \'is defined\' is a boolean check.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the issue is in the \'block\' structure. Let me check the YAML syntax for blocks and \'when\' conditions.\n\nIn YAML, a \'block\' can have \'when\' at the same level as the tasks. So, the structure is correct.\n\nWait, perhaps the issue is that the \'when\' is written as a string without being properly enclosed. Let me check: in YAML, \'when\' can be a string representing a Jinja2 expression, so it\'s correctly written.\n\nI think I might have to proceed with the line length fix and see if that\'s the only issue, but the user mentioned two errors. So, perhaps the truthy value issue is elsewhere.\n\nWait, perhaps the \'when\' in the \'Install latest hashicorp product using packag